    "text": "<p>Here, gain in kinetic energy<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo></math>loss in potential energy</p><p>Now loss in potential energy of particle in falling from height&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi></math>&nbsp;to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math>.</p><p>So,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#916;</mi><mi>K</mi><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>K</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Thus, kinetic energy at point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math></p>"
